KNOWNBUG buechi
always_with_range2.sv
--buechi --bound 10
^\[main\.p0\] always \(always \[0:2\] main\.c != 5\): REFUTED$
^\[main\.p1\] always \(always \[1:2\] main\.c != 5\): REFUTED$
^\[main\.p2\] always \(always \[1:\$\] main\.c != 5\): REFUTED$
^\[main\.p3\] always \(main\.c == 2 \|-> \(always \[0:2\] main\.c != 4\)\): REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
ltl_sva_to_stringt::rec (src/temporal-logic/ltl_sva_to_string.cpp)
emits sva_ranged_always as the Spot operator F[a:b] (bounded
eventually) instead of G[a:b] (bounded always).  The Buechi automaton
therefore encodes "eventually [a:b]", and EBMC reports PROVED for all
four properties with --buechi.  The non-Buechi word-level BMC encoding
gives the correct result.
